id: pm-jev-k8qe
title: Batch open backlog triage with bounded streaming and stable receipts
description: "Implement open backlog selection, one run deadline, compact per-item streaming, content receipt reuse, stale inference protection, minimal projection and direct packed install acceptance."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[1]: "pkg:pm-jev"
created_at: "2026-10-11T05:08:46.971Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-11T06:25:57.776Z"
author: codex-sol-implementation
parent: pm-jev-0w3q
comments[11]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-11T05:09:51.100Z",codex-sol-implementation,"Implementation scope: bounded open backlog selection and one deadline; compact streaming; full source hashes and redacted apply receipts; stale inference checks; smaller triage state; supported Ollama keep_alive; direct tarball acceptance. Existing reconciliation items remain owned by the orchestrator. Live model calls are waiting for baseline completion."
  "2026-10-11T05:20:38.930Z",codex-sol-implementation,"Inspected the host authoring contracts: streaming uses public writeStdout and suppressHostOutput, while SDK read output controls are static rather than an asynchronous item iterator. Ollama systemone accepts shared state plus named questions and no independent-state batch or streaming response. Reuse one boundary/client/catalog and one run AbortSignal across sequential item requests. The official TypeSafe SDK forwards additional request properties, so Ollama keep_alive uses its actual systemone wire field without a custom transport. Existing triage already used one systemOne call for four questions. Hosted opt-in and redirect refusal remain enforced."
  "2026-10-11T05:32:07.365Z",codex-sol-implementation,"Implementation uses complete untruncated source SHA-256 for receipt reuse, plus a redacted inference revision hash and expiry checked by the host mutation guard under the item lock. Source reuse ignores inferred type/priority and annotations so apply does not invalidate its receipt. Tests bind real scratch clients with createExtensionCommandSdk and initialize real trackers through PmClient.init, avoiding repeated CLI boot overhead and accidental package-workspace scope. Packed acceptance uses deterministic loopback HTTP and direct archive installation; real model acceptance remains separate and has not run."
  "2026-10-11T05:49:17.371Z",codex-sol-implementation,"Behavioral revert proof in a scratch package copy: preserved working source, changed only projectTriageState to the earlier broad projection and triageSourceHash to a hash of truncated projected input. Rebuilt dist with npm run build, then ran node --test test/triage-dist.test.ts unchanged: exit 1, 0 passed, 3 failed, 0 skipped or canceled. Failures were minimal wire evidence, routing-stable full-content identity, and repeat apply making two HTTP requests instead of one. Restored the two functions byte-for-byte, rebuilt dist and reran the same command: exit 0, 3 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped or canceled. No exports or tests were removed."
  "2026-10-11T05:55:16.127Z",codex-sol-implementation,"The linked real-tracker regression command passed 11 tests with zero failures, cancellations or skips. The host reported test-result tracking disabled; no project policy was changed. Whole-source coverage exposed one remaining generic host-error branch, now covered with deletion during inference. Packed acceptance uses deterministic loopback responses and direct archive installation for npm and native Bun; no live model request has been made."
  "2026-10-11T05:58:31.118Z",codex-sol-implementation,"Correction to the preceding coverage note: deletion during inference preserves the host item_deleted code; a separate strict ownership refusal exercises the code-less expected error fallback. Synthetic duplicate-description projection measured 4307 bytes before versus 2164 bytes after (49.76 percent smaller JSON state); this is input-size evidence, not live latency or token-use evidence. Live measurements remain owned by the orchestrator."
  "2026-10-11T06:01:33.771Z",codex-sol-implementation,The final generic-error regression removes only a scratch source document while the deterministic HTTP response is pending. The real host raises a code-less missing-item error; the batch emits jev_triage_failure and writes no receipt. A separate SDK deletion case retains item_deleted. Both tests preserve native SDK behavior without PM mocks. Prior exploratory ownership fixtures were replaced rather than weakening coverage thresholds.
  "2026-10-11T06:05:37.031Z",codex-sol-implementation,"The host-linked command PM_AUTHOR=codex-sol-implementation pm --no-extensions test pm-jev-k8qe --run --progress passed its then-current 13 regressions, zero failed, canceled or skipped. Deleted/missing source cases were subsequently consolidated into one table-driven regression to preserve the existing zero-duplication gate; both native failure branches remain covered. The batch documentation is included in package files so the README link works for installed consumers."
  "2026-10-11T06:11:54.674Z",codex-sol-implementation,"npm run release:check passed: 127 tests passed, zero failed/canceled/skipped; native and c8 whole-source coverage 100 percent across all 11 TypeScript source files; 214 documented declarations; zero duplicate lines across 29 checked sources; production audit zero vulnerabilities; 14 packed files including batch documentation; changelog and publication attestation checks passed. Bun and isolated identity gates are still pending. npm ci initially reported four high development advisories already covered by existing tracking; no existing reconciliation item was modified."
  "2026-10-11T06:21:06.960Z",codex-sol-implementation,"bun run release:check passed with 127 passed tests, zero failures/cancellations/skips and 100 percent whole-source lines/branches/functions across 11 source files. npm run test:install passed one complete acceptance scenario: direct archive npm/Bun imports, bundled documentation, direct host installation, Node and native Bun triage, compact/full output, gate exits, batch JSON lines, apply, zero-request Bun receipt reuse, changed-source skip and real item-lock refusal. Consumers use matching host SDK 2026.10.10. Earlier dependency provisioning stalled; the successful final run used a bounded install timeout with forced termination on expiry. No live model requests were run. Isolated identity gate remains pending."
  "2026-10-11T06:25:43.933Z",codex-sol-implementation,"Final isolated gate passed with HOME=$(mktemp -d) GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 npm run release:check: 127 passed, zero failed/canceled/skipped, 100 percent whole-source coverage across 11 files, clean production audit, unchanged thresholds and passing packaging/changelog/attestation checks. All three requested release gates passed. Final scope includes implementation, generated dist, TypeScript regressions, minimal projection, source-stable receipts, lock-scoped freshness/deadline refusal and direct tarball docs/acceptance. Live acceptance is added behind test:live but was not run; measured model latency remains external. SDK limits: shared-state systemOne has no independent-state batch or response streaming, and tracker operations do not accept cancellation. CLI orientation reported list-open deprecated; linked test-result persistence is disabled by existing project policy. No push, PR, release, tag or existing reconciliation mutation was performed; this feature remains in progress for orchestrator verification."
